# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Before this file existed, 191 tracked files were committed with CRLF, which cost
# portfolio-api 5,725 ESLint errors (`prettier/prettier`: Delete ␍) and left every
# shell script with a broken shebang. `.prettierrc` already declares
# "endOfLine": "lf", so prettier and git agree.
*                text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts are stated explicitly rather than left to the default above.
# This is the case where getting it wrong is functional, not cosmetic: a CRLF
# shebang fails on Linux with `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M`.
*.sh             text eol=lf

# Binary formats. `* text=auto` would very likely classify these correctly on its
# own; an explicit guard is the difference between "probably fine" and "cannot be
# corrupted by a future renormalization".
*.png            binary
*.jpg            binary
*.jpeg           binary
*.webp           binary
*.avif           binary
*.ico            binary
*.pdf            binary
*.woff           binary
*.woff2          binary
